308	  `instructions` can be a string, an object, or an array. Start with a string. Use an object when the question needs data alongside it, such as a record to compare the state against, or when part of the question is built by your code. [Use structure in the questions](/concepts/how-to-build-with-system-one#use-structure-in-the-questions) explains when structure helps, and [the example below](#structured-instructions) shows it with questions built in code.
