517	Each answer is the probability that the resume is for the person in that record. Record 18 spells the name differently but matches on location and employer, and gets 0.74. Record 42 has the same name in a different city with a different employer, and gets 0.09. Record 77 is a similar name at the same location with a different employer, and gets 0.08. Threshold each value in your code, as in [Handling multiple Noul answers in code](#handling-multiple-noul-answers-in-code), and send the middle values to a person.
518	
519	With the Python SDK, the questions are built from the candidate records. The question text is fixed and the record changes:
520	
521	```python theme={null}
522	from typesafe_sdk import Noul, TypeSafeClient
523	
524	SAME_PERSON = "Is the resume for the same person as `potential_duplicate`?"
525	
526	
527	def duplicate_questions(candidates: list[dict]) -> dict[str, Noul]:
528	    """One Noul per candidate record, all asking the same question."""
529	    return {
530	        f"same_as_record_{candidate['id']}": Noul(
531	            instructions={
532	                "potential_duplicate": {
533	                    "name": candidate["name"],
534	                    "location": candidate["location"],
535	                    "last_employer": candidate["last_employer"],
536	                },
537	                "question": SAME_PERSON,
538	            },
539	        )
540	        for candidate in candidates
541	    }
542	
543	
544	def find_duplicates(resume: dict, candidates: list[dict]) -> list[str]:
545	    with TypeSafeClient() as client:
546	        response = client.system_one(
547	            model="jev-latest",
548	            state={"resume": resume},
549	            questions=duplicate_questions(candidates),
550	        )
551	    return [
552	        question_id
553	        for question_id, answer in response.answers.items()
554	        if answer.noul > 0.7
555	    ]
556	```
557	
558	The [structured-data-extraction cascade cookbook](/cookbooks/sde_cascade) uses structured instructions to verify an extracted record. Every field gets the same set of questions. Each question's `instructions` object has the question text in the `main_question` property. There are also `field_spec` and `extracted_field` properties that change for each field.
559	
560	## Noul in the cookbooks
561	
562	Take a look at our cookbooks to see apps using Noul questions:
563	
564	* [Parallel questions](/cookbooks/parallel_questions) runs a 13-question regulatory checklist over one article in a single request.
565	* [Self-consistency: nouls](/cookbooks/consistency_noul_cookbook) scores an insurance claim against a 15-question rubric and measures how stable the values are across runs.
566	* [Re-ranking](/cookbooks/rerank_typesafe) uses the probability itself, not a threshold: one Noul per query-candidate pair, then sorts candidates by the value.
567	* [Line-by-line search](/cookbooks/semantic_find) pairs a Choice that finds the matching line with a Noul that checks whether the document contains an answer at all.
568	* [Structure recovery](/cookbooks/autoformat) asks one Noul per pair of lines, whether a line break split a sentence, to rebuild paragraphs from plain text.
