872	
873	The three scales have different lengths, so before combining them, normalize each score. A four-level scale returns 0 to 3 and a three-level scale returns 0 to 2, so a top score on one is bigger than a top score on the other. Divide each score by its top level number, `len(criteria) - 1`, to put every score on 0 to 1. Then the weights mean what they say: 0.6 on severity and 0.3 on frustration makes severity count twice as much.
